{{!
    @template tiny_codelab/cloud_usage

    The plan and the usage of this month of a hosted runner, on the settings page (from GET /usage of the runner).

    Context variables required for this template:
    * level - info, warning (80 % of the runs or 7 days left) or danger (nothing runs any more)
    * bar - colour of the bar: success, warning or danger
    * percent - share of the runs of the month used, 0 to 100
    * plan - the plan and its status
    * runs - the runs of this month and the quota
    * detail - editor sessions, quiz grading and programs at once
    * expires - the end date and the days left (may be empty)
    * server - the site id and the server of the connection key (may be empty)

    @copyright  2026 Boban Blagojević
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later

    Example context (json):
    {
        "level": "info",
        "bar": "success",
        "percent": 12,
        "plan": "Plan: Trial. Status: active.",
        "runs": "Runs this month: 240 of 2,000 (12%).",
        "detail": "Editor sessions: 220. Quiz grading: 20. Programs at once: up to 10.",
        "expires": "Active until 25 December 2026, 30 days left.",
        "server": "Site id book-proba on the server cloud.codelabedu.com."
    }
}}
<div class="tiny_codelab-cloudusage alert alert-{{level}} mb-0">
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between">
        <strong class="me-3">{{plan}}</strong>
        <span>{{runs}}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="progress my-2" style="height: .5rem;">
        <div class="progress-bar bg-{{bar}}" role="progressbar" style="width: {{percent}}%;" aria-valuenow="{{percent}}"
            aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-label="{{runs}}"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="small">{{detail}}</div>
    {{#expires}}<div class="small">{{expires}}</div>{{/expires}}
    {{#server}}<div class="small text-muted">{{server}}</div>{{/server}}
</div>
